.TH SDL_StringToGUID 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_StringToGUID \- Convert a GUID string into a
.BR SDL_GUID
structure.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_guid.h>
.PP
.BI "SDL_GUID SDL_StringToGUID(const char *pchGUID);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Performs no error checking\[char46] If this function is given a string containing an invalid GUID, the function will silently succeed, but the GUID generated will not be useful\[char46]

.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I pchGUID
string containing an ASCII representation of a GUID\[char46]
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns a
.BR SDL_GUID
structure\[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
It is safe to call this function from any thread\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR SDL_GUIDToString (3)
